Subject: dxgi/dcomp: namespace the composition-swapchain window property by pid

The composition swapchain to composition window mapping is published as
a property on the desktop window, keyed by the swapchain object's
address. The desktop window's property list is shared across the whole
window station, so two processes that allocate a swapchain at the same
address (a host app and its WebView2 child, Live's exact shape) collide
on the key, and a lookup in one resolves another process's window.

Key the property by the owning process id together with the address.
The format string lives once in include/wine/winedxgi.idl so the dxgi
setter and the dcomp getter cannot drift apart silently.

Ported from giang17/wine df092626; six of its seven sites exist in this
tree, the seventh belongs to the fork's tree compositor.

